    q: 'How much does a clinical research associate earn in India?',
    a: 'Entry-level Junior CRA or CRA I roles typically pay roughly Rs 3.5-6.5 LPA. CRA II or Senior CRA roles, usually reached around 3-6 years of experience, pay roughly Rs 8-14 LPA. Lead CRA or Clinical Trial Manager roles reach roughly Rs 16-22 LPA. These are directional ranges pulled from current salary-tracking sources and vary by city, employer type (CRO versus sponsor versus hospital), and therapeutic-area specialisation.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is clinical research a growing field in India right now?',
    a: 'Yes. India registered close to 18,000 new clinical trials in 2024, roughly 50% growth over the previous year, and the market grew at a compound annual growth rate of around 80% between 2019 and 2024, making India the third-largest clinical trials destination globally. India\'s clinical trials market is projected to keep expanding through 2030, driven by faster CDSCO approval timelines and rising sponsor interest in Indian trial sites.',
  },
